==================================================================
DAY 51 - PART B: LAB
Package your app as a Helm chart and as Kustomize overlays
Time: 120 minutes
==================================================================

PART 1: HELM CHART
==================

STEP 1: Scaffold
----------------
mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/week8/charts && cd $_
helm create myapp
tree myapp
Read templates/deployment.yaml and _helpers.tpl. Note how names and
labels come from helpers.


STEP 2: Adapt values.yaml to your app
-------------------------------------
Edit myapp/values.yaml:
  image:
    repository: YOURUSER/myapp
    tag: "v4"
  service:
    port: 80
  containerPort: 5000
  greeting: "Hello from my chart"
  resources:
    requests: {cpu: 50m, memory: 64Mi}
    limits: {memory: 128Mi}
  ingress:
    enabled: true
    className: nginx
    hosts:
    - host: myapp.local
      paths:
      - path: /
        pathType: Prefix
  autoscaling:
    enabled: false

Edit Chart.yaml: appVersion: "v4", description.


STEP 3: Templates
-----------------
In templates/deployment.yaml:
  - set containerPort to {{ .Values.containerPort }}
  - change liveness path to /healthz and readiness path to /ready
  - add env from a ConfigMap:
          envFrom:
          - configMapRef:
              name: {{ include "myapp.fullname" . }}
  - add under spec.template.metadata.annotations:
          checksum/config: {{ include (print $.Template.BasePath "/configmap.yaml") . | sha256sum }}
In templates/service.yaml set targetPort: {{ .Values.containerPort }}.

Create templates/configmap.yaml:

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ include "myapp.fullname" . }}
  labels:
    {{- include "myapp.labels" . | nindent 4 }}
data:
  GREETING: {{ .Values.greeting | quote }}


STEP 4: Lint, render, install
-----------------------------
helm lint myapp
helm template t myapp | less
helm install myapp ./myapp -n app-dev --create-namespace
k get all,ingress,cm -n app-dev
curl -s -H "Host: myapp.local" localhost


STEP 5: Environments
--------------------
cat > values-prod.yaml <<EOF
replicaCount: 3
greeting: "Hello from PROD"
ingress:
  hosts:
  - host: myapp-prod.local
    paths:
    - path: /
      pathType: Prefix
EOF
helm upgrade --install myapp-prod ./myapp -n app-prod --create-namespace -f values-prod.yaml
curl -s -H "Host: myapp-prod.local" localhost

Change the greeting and upgrade: pods roll automatically thanks to
the checksum annotation.
  helm upgrade myapp-prod ./myapp -n app-prod -f values-prod.yaml --set greeting="changed"
  k get pods -n app-prod -w


STEP 6: Package
---------------
helm package myapp          # myapp-0.1.0.tgz
(Optional: push to an OCI registry:
 helm push myapp-0.1.0.tgz oci://registry-1.docker.io/YOURUSER)

helm uninstall myapp -n app-dev ; helm uninstall myapp-prod -n app-prod
k delete ns app-dev app-prod


PART 2: KUSTOMIZE
=================

STEP 7: Base
------------
mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/week8/kustomize/{base,overlays/dev,overlays/prod} && cd ~/k8s-journey/week8/kustomize

base/deployment.yaml: Deployment "myapp" (1 replica, image myapp,
  port 5000, requests, probes /healthz and /ready, envFrom configMap
  "app-config")
base/service.yaml: Service "myapp" 80 -> 5000
base/kustomization.yaml:

apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization
resources:
- deployment.yaml
- service.yaml
labels:
- pairs:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: myapp
  includeSelectors: true
configMapGenerator:
- name: app-config
  literals:
  - GREETING=Hello from base


STEP 8: Dev overlay
-------------------
overlays/dev/kustomization.yaml:

apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization
namespace: kz-dev
resources:
- ../../base
- namespace.yaml
images:
- name: myapp
  newName: docker.io/YOURUSER/myapp
  newTag: v4
configMapGenerator:
- name: app-config
  behavior: merge
  literals:
  - GREETING=Hello from DEV

overlays/dev/namespace.yaml: a Namespace kz-dev.

k kustomize overlays/dev        # read the output: namespace, image,
                                # configmap name with hash suffix
k apply -k overlays/dev
k get all,cm -n kz-dev


STEP 9: Prod overlay with patches
---------------------------------
overlays/prod/kustomization.yaml:

apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization
namespace: kz-prod
resources:
- ../../base
- namespace.yaml
images:
- name: myapp
  newName: docker.io/YOURUSER/myapp
  newTag: v4
replicas:
- name: myapp
  count: 3
configMapGenerator:
- name: app-config
  behavior: merge
  literals:
  - GREETING=Hello from PROD
patches:
- path: patch-resources.yaml

overlays/prod/patch-resources.yaml:

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: myapp
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: myapp
        resources:
          requests: {cpu: 200m, memory: 128Mi}
          limits: {memory: 256Mi}

(The container name in the patch must match base/deployment.yaml.)

k diff -k overlays/prod ; k apply -k overlays/prod
k get pods -n kz-prod


STEP 10: Change config -> automatic rollout
-------------------------------------------
Change GREETING in overlays/prod, re-apply. The ConfigMap gets a new
hashed name, the Deployment reference changes, pods roll.
  k get cm -n kz-prod ; k get pods -n kz-prod -w

Change the image tag the CI way:
  cd overlays/prod && kustomize edit set image myapp=docker.io/YOURUSER/myapp:v3 && cd -
  (needs the kustomize CLI; or edit newTag by hand)


STEP 11: Clean up and commit
----------------------------
k delete -k overlays/dev ; k delete -k overlays/prod
cd ~/k8s-journey && git add . && git commit -m "day51: own chart and kustomize"
